  "notes": "{招|まね}く is a transitive godan verb with meanings ranging from \"to invite\" to \"to cause.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く\n\nUSAGE:\n1. To invite (people): ⟦{客|きゃく}→客：00865_kyaku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く (invite guests)\n2. To beckon: ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{招|まね}く (wave someone over)\n3. To cause/bring about: ⟦{災|わざわ}い→災い：27851_wazawai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く (invite trouble)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{誤解|ごかい}→誤解：02769_gokai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く: to cause a misunderstanding\n- ⟦{批判|ひはん}→批判：03580_hihan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く: to invite criticism\n- ⟦{注目|ちゅうもく}→注目：03483_chuumoku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{招|まね}く: to attract attention\n- ⟦{招待|しょうたい}する→招待する：01833_shoutaisuru⟧: to invite (formal)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\n⟦{招|まね}き{猫|ねこ}→招き猫：06538_manekineko⟧ (beckoning cat) is a lucky charm placed at shop entrances to invite customers and good fortune.",
